  "body": "## Accepted full original lower-bound target\n\nProblem 30002170 / OWR-12013-003, first substantive approach 1/5. The original lower-bound target is accepted after independent AI mathematical audit and acceptance review: for every fixed H in (1/4,1), every T>0 and every integer n>=1, the optimal conditional-expectation RMS error for the canonical iterated integral is at least c_H T^(2H) n^(1/2-2H), with c_H>0 depending only on H. Both independent standard fractional Brownian components are observed at every uniform sample time. The proof applies to every square-integrable observation-measurable estimator.\n\nThe rough range 1/4<H<1/2 is the substantive residual. The exact Brownian optimum and smooth-range asymptotic optimal rate remain credited known cases. No historical novelty/priority certificate, sharp constant, exact normalized-error limit, endpoint result, or adaptive/arbitrary-mesh extension is claimed.\n\n## Complete proofs and mathematical audit\n\nThe edition preserves the complete localized Gaussian-witness proof, its all-H extension, the full Euler-to-polygonal canonical-convention proof, and the full independent mathematical audit. The audit retains all essential reasoning, including Fourier normalization, regularity and periodization, independence from both sampled components, signed-PSD-trace variance control, finite-identity/L2 passage, and joint-law transfer from the auxiliary Gaussian realization. Every displayed formula in these four mathematical documents is preserved byte for byte. No mandatory mathematical repair was needed.\n\nCandidate/pending status is updated to scoped full-target acceptance. All material is AI-assisted and unrefereed; acceptance is not external human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification. The explicitly identified established area-convergence theorem and standard Gaussian/Fourier foundations remain inputs.\n\n## Attribution and publication boundary\n\nThe original problem is credited to [Neuenkirch's OWR contribution](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2012/41), pp.2524\u20132525. The convergence input is [Neuenkirch\u2013Tindel\u2013Unterberger](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spa.2009.10.007), with the inspected [arXiv version](https://arxiv.org/abs/0902.0497) explicitly identified. The prior smooth-H result is credited to [Neuenkirch\u2013Shalaiko](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jco.2015.09.008).\n\nExactly nine authored proof/audit/metadata files are added under unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30002170/. No QUEUE or historical-accounting changes, source bodies/extracts/images, datasets, scripts/checkers, computational outputs/logs, private sources or coordination material are included. Optional finite-check and Brownian numerical-consistency paragraphs are omitted; no omitted computation is converted into prose. Public scholarly PDF identities and retrieval/inspection metadata, manuscript-version distinctions, and bounded-source/novelty limitations remain explicit. Edition preparation makes no new retrieval, PDF-rehash, source-inspection or literature-search claim.\n\nStrict local clean-patch replay and native Git blob/tree identity checks passed. The complete expected tree chain preserves every unrelated entry. These local checks do not claim remote verification or CI success. Draft review publication only; no merge, release, DOI, or outside outreach.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `ALL_H_COROLLARY.md`: 3,294 bytes; SHA-256 `08c222ad9bf5451745a21d3fbb10ddceca49eefec141f0f913b32802fc1badff`.\n- `AREA_CONVENTION_CHECK.md`: 2,901 bytes; SHA-256 `13f534584f5939a3a198ae34134847376e4d0aec22b9112b9390b41cfab3d6db`.\n- `INDEPENDENT_AUDIT.md`: 19,070 bytes; SHA-256 `71c2e9a16afa176968b12b8cbce625da6444ebb8fb08025267ec209e98516042`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,755 bytes; SHA-256 `7a82788014bce405e27b16501d9e18956217a4017865594a59cade40efe91581`.\n- `PROOF.md`: 11,413 bytes; SHA-256 `95f7e49ce01784aa9e63b6a0c735230056a17cb8e37764689b630f8da71459f1`.\n- `PROVENANCE.md`: 3,788 bytes; SHA-256 `05e41ac374400e709e961e6c52e431f115a484884d7986691d6c32f4bcc4e6da`.\n- `README.md`: 3,043 bytes; SHA-256 `063d7815f71c1ee0ce930d8f204a05cdd6ba2d0239189ec049d183b551b8fae2`.\n- `SOURCE_LEDGER.md`: 5,991 bytes; SHA-256 `028c00ad283d6722bee8279c42ee6a275e7b5d3148e21496b27f28cdea381f58`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,581 bytes; SHA-256 `cb078ab06b98f274cecfab7f9f1eb1192f01db5acab6c3b99114393cdb081bfc`.\n\nThe manifest lists nine members and hashes the other eight; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
